# Design system — Modern Scorebook Utility

This is an original Crease system. `docs/UI.md` and the shipped tokens are the
only visual source of truth. Do not regenerate screens from external design
tools or revive superseded palettes.

## When implementing or updating UI

1. Prefer `docs/UI.md` + current tokens.
2. Rebuild with reusable React components; do not paste generated HTML.
3. Keep `src/styles/globals.css` and `src/constants/design-tokens.ts` in sync.
4. Prefer shared tokens/components over per-screen utilities.

## Typography

| Role | Face | Via |
|---|---|---|
| Headlines, match titles, dates, fees, counts, scores | **Oswald** | `font-heading` + shared typography |
| Body, labels, forms, nav | **Plus Jakarta Sans** | `--font-sans` + shared typography |

Use `Display`, `Headline`, `Title`, `Stat`, `Label`, `Overline`, `Caption`,
`Body`, and `BodySm`. Keep operational copy at 12px or larger. Use one `h1`
per route.

## Color

| Token | Light | Dark (Neutral Night) | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| Canvas | `#F2F2F1` | `#0C0E0D` | Page background |
| Ink primary | `#1A1A1A` | `#EDEEEB` | Primary actions / brand |
| Clubhouse | `#0A0C0B` | `#0A0C0B` | Match tickets / brand mark |
| Amber accent | `#E0B84A` | `#E0B84A` | Selected state **only** |
| Urgency red | `#C44B42` | `#E5736A` | Unpaid / destructive |
| Success blue | `#1A6BB5` | `#7EB6E0` | Confirmations |

Never use green or lime for brand, actions, success, or chrome. Do not paint
neutral hover surfaces amber.

The official app artwork is a minimal amber C-shaped hand cradling an off-white
cricket ball on clubhouse black. Its master source is
`scripts/crease-app-logo-source.png`; generate every favicon, Apple icon, and
PWA icon with `npm run icons:generate`. Do not add small secondary symbols.

## Layout and interaction

- Touch targets are at least 48px; documented dense exceptions are at least 40px.
- Radius defaults to 8px; use tonal surfaces and hairline dividers.
- Mobile nav is exactly Home, Matches, Team, Pay, Profile.
- Desktop uses the sidebar and may expose Fund and Settings directly.
- Prefer bottom sheets for mobile create, confirm, pay, and management flows.
- Toasts, push banners, sheets, keyboard, and bottom nav use shared geometry tokens.
- Avoid gradients, glassmorphism, nested cards, decorative clipart, and heavy shadows.

## Signature patterns

- **App artwork** — same themed master in app chrome and every icon output.
- **MatchTicket** — dominant next-fixture surface.
- **MatchPollControl** — shared compact/full one-tap voting control.
- **SegmentedControl** — amber active state for exclusive choices.
- **ManageMatchSheet** — staged Admin lifecycle actions.
- **MetricRail** — compact operational metrics.
- **BottomSheet** — mobile-first task and confirmation container.
